; ========================================================
; DNS EMAIL SECURITY & SPOOFING DEFENSE RECORDS
; Add these TXT and CAA records to your DNS zone file or registrar
; ========================================================

; 1. SPF (Sender Policy Framework) - Protects against unauthorized email senders
@    IN    TXT    "v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all"

; (If this domain sends NO email at all, use this strict null SPF record instead):
; @    IN    TXT    "v=spf1 -all"

; 2. DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance)
; Enforces quarantine/reject on spoofed emails and sends daily telemetry
_dmarc    IN    TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=reject; sp=reject; adkim=s; aspf=s; pct=100; rua=mailto:dmarc-reports@yourdomain.com"

; 3. CAA (Certificate Authority Authorization) - Prevents unauthorized SSL cert issuance
@    IN    CAA    0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
@    IN    CAA    0 issue "digicert.com"
@    IN    CAA    0 iodef "mailto:security@yourdomain.com"
